स्मरण किसका है?
Who is Remembering What?

When the mind is fascinated by the countless names, forms, memories and desires of the world, it overlooks the ever-present Self.

When attention returns to its own Source, the world does not vanish—it simply loses its power to veil Reality.

The world may continue to appear.

The body may continue to act.

Thoughts may continue to arise.

Yet the false notion,

"I am this limited individual,"

comes to rest.

This is why the sages do not teach us to reject the world.

They teach us to see it in its true light.

The Self is never absent.

It does not need to be remembered as though it had been lost.

Only the habit of overlooking It comes to an end.

Then, without effort,

silence remains,

awareness remains,

love remains,

and the world is recognized as a passing appearance in the one indivisible Consciousness.

As the Yoga Vāsiṣṭha repeatedly reminds us,

The disappearance of ignorance—not the disappearance of the world—is liberation.

हरिः ॐ तत्सत्।
